Name     Keshari Academy Program Service Room~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob~Desc     This sealed service room exists for academy mobile programs and should not be
removed. Maintenance labels identify it as part of Keshari Hunter Academy's
internal automation network.
~

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50700
Name     Keshari Academy Test Workshop~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob factory~Desc     A small test workshop used by academy staff. Benches, diagnostic ports and
compact sensor stations and tactical displays built for rapid situational
awareness fill the room.
~

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50701
Name     Keshari Quiet Test Compartment~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob safe silence~Desc     A deliberately quiet compartment isolated from the busier academy modules.
subdued directional lighting that leaves no distracting glare and sound-damped
surfaces make it suitable for testing or study.
~

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50729
Name     Keshari Isolated Test Chamber~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob prototype~Desc     This isolated test chamber is intentionally featureless. Instrument panels
from compact sensor stations and tactical displays built for rapid situational
awareness are the only obvious connection to the rest of Keshari Hunter
Academy.
~

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50730
Name     Keshari Student Commons~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob safe~
Desc     This is the academy student commons, a final safe place to rest, read and
practice using the message system. Use NOTE LIST to list messages, NOTE READ
<msgnum> to read one, and HELP NOTE for additional commands.

The room is a quiet den-like commons with alcoves for small groups and
solitary study. The station windows give occasional views of the muted surface
of Ross 128 b framed by the station's narrow observation ports.
~
